  "description": "\nThe interior refurb project scope meant it was non notifiable but all CDM regulations have been met, assisted by our specialist sub-contractor No Nonsense CDM Ltd.\n\nThis application relates to the restrospective request for advertising consent (my clients were previously advised that the Landlord team’s approval would be sufficient within the development) and a proposed new storage grille/access door to create a secure storage area that also mitigates the risk to life and property posed by the homeless people sleeping there while under the influence.\n\nThe intention is to provide the area with a new, secure storage enclosure that is aesthetically sympathetic to the existing service areas.   Whilst also providing an external storage area for my client’s operations.  Proposed exterior power, fire detection and CCTV will be IP Rated.  The Landlord also has an existing CCTV camera, also indicated on the drawings. \n\nSignage has already been installed but we did take precedence from Elliot's, who have two sources of illumination on their shopfront also.\n",
  "subdivision_of_building": "Ground floor unit exterior signage and proposed new storage enclosure to area adjacent.",
  "actual_completion_date": null,
  "lpa_app_no": "2025/0235",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "application_type_full": "Full planning & display of advertisements",
  "last_updated_by": "Planning Portal ingest",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "id": "Hackney-2025_0235",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;1. No advertisement is to be displayed without the permission of the owner of the site or any other person with an interest in the site entitled to grant permission.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;2. No advertisement shall be sited or displayed so as to&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left: 25px;&quot;&gt; (a)endanger persons using any highway, railway, waterway, dock, harbour or aerodrome (civil or military);&lt;br&gt;(b)obscure, or hinder the ready interpretation of, any traffic sign, railway signal or aid to navigation by water or air; or&lt;br&gt;(c)hinder the operation of any device used for the purpose of security or surveillance or for measuring the speed of any vehicle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;3. Any advertisement displayed, and any site used for the display of advertisements, shall be maintained in a condition that does not impair the visual amenity of the site.\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n4. Any structure or hoarding erected or used principally for the purpose of displaying advertisements shall be maintained in a condition that does not endanger the public.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n5. Where an advertisement is required under these Regulations to be removed, the site shall be left in a condition that does not endanger the public or impair visual amenity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To safeguard amenity and public safety.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
